Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.61,0:00:04.75,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The true flow, orderly yet free, \Ncan be neither stopped nor controlled.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.75,0:00:06.44,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,In like fashion, this sturdy lock, too,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.83,0:00:08.54,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,shall disperse to its original flow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.54,0:00:09.32,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.32,0:00:11.67,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I shun thee away, force that acted as lock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.48,0:00:34.54,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Now then, can I bring her back \Nwithout waking her up?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.15,0:02:10.98,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Pride of the Past ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.98,0:02:13.19,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,Magdalsia    {\fs14}Farmland Nation South of Tuldarr
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.14,0:02:13.19,Default-Top,Gemma,0,0,0,,My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.59,0:02:15.28,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,King Hubert!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.28,0:02:17.74,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,Hubert    {\fs14}King of Magdalsia
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.00,0:02:19.24,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Someone!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.24,0:02:21.18,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Someone, come at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.42,0:02:28.37,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,King Hubert of Magdalsia \Nhas mysteriously fallen into a coma.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.89,0:02:32.16,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,He remains unconscious, \Ndespite no apparent abnormalities,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.16,0:02:33.80,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,so they suspect magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.34,0:02:37.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I won't be able to tell \Nunless I take a look myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.94,0:02:40.45,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Should we have an envoy investigate the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.45,0:02:43.13,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, it'd be too dangerous \Ngiven what little we know.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.13,0:02:44.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be the one to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.51,0:02:47.01,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Your Majesty will visit in person?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.01,0:02:48.73,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,What if it's a trap?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.73,0:02:51.19,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll have people accompany me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.32,0:02:56.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The most important person \Nin Tuldarr right now is Legis.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.98,0:02:59.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm nothing but a temporary ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.13,0:03:01.81,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.81,0:03:06.21,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,But please let the king of Farsas \Nknow before you depart.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.21,0:03:08.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Ugh, seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.62,0:03:10.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The very thought makes me sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.27,0:03:13.21,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Isn't it better than having him \Nfind out and get angry?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.17,0:03:18.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So that sums it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.51,0:03:21.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be off to Magdalsia no—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.00,0:03:23.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,"That sums it up," my foot.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.11,0:03:25.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Listen here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.41,0:03:29.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's almost the new year, \Nwith just over a month until our wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.09,0:03:31.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why must you stick your nose \Nin this fishy business?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.23,0:03:34.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They're the ones who asked us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.24,0:03:35.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Ignore them. Don't go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.61,0:03:37.57,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I-I can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.57,0:03:40.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Magdalsia is Tuldarr's neighbor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.43,0:03:43.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Time is of the essence with a life at stake.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.24,0:03:45.16,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll just go and take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.16,0:03:48.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How much trouble have you gotten \Nyourself into doing exactly that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.08,0:03:54.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You let me know beforehand, \Nso I'll consider that progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.85,0:03:56.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Make sure you take your spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.72,0:03:58.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So I can go, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.29,0:04:00.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's an affair that involves Tuldarr, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.51,0:04:02.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I have no right to stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.01,0:04:04.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be back before you know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.05,0:04:06.54,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.69,0:04:11.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I swear, she really is a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.32,0:04:15.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Senn. Senn?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.52,0:04:17.86,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,That's strange. There's no way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.86,0:04:20.99,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,A spirit can't ignore \Na summons from Lady Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.99,0:04:22.95,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,That goes against the contract!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.95,0:04:24.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Wh-What now?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.83,0:04:26.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Could something have happened to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.01,0:04:30.32,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,The contract is still in place, \Nso I don't think he's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.62,0:04:33.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Itz, Karr, Saiha.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.05,0:04:36.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Can you go look for Senn?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.79,0:04:45.51,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,My apologies for having you come all this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.51,0:04:48.56,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)\pos(273,295)}Gemma    {\fs14}Queen of Magdalsia
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.02,0:04:49.22,Default-Top,Gemma,0,0,0,,We can't figure out what could have caused it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.22,0:04:51.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's no trouble at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.52,0:04:55.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It is part of Tuldarr's duties \Nto resolve magic-related issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.15,0:05:01.50,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Who might you be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.50,0:05:03.94,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,You're intruding in here without my consent!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.94,0:05:06.16,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,How do you do, Gemma?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.50,0:05:09.16,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,There's no need to concern yourself \Nwith the king's health.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.57,0:05:11.12,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,He's only sleeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.33,0:05:14.79,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,I demand to know who you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.79,0:05:16.69,Default-Top,Lucia,0,0,0,,My name is Lucia.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.46,0:05:18.42,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(700,500)\pos(467,300)}Lucia
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.69,0:05:20.29,Default-Top,Lucia,0,0,0,,I'm here to act as a proxy \Nwhile the king is asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.29,0:05:21.45,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,A proxy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.61,0:05:29.31,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,No, this can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.31,0:05:31.48,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,You can see that's the king's handwriting.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.48,0:05:34.22,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,I've been given full power and authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.22,0:05:39.06,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,If His Majesty really {\i1}is{\i0} safe, \NI'd like for him to tell me what's going on!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.06,0:05:40.82,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.62,0:05:44.53,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Gemma, do you not understand your situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.70,0:05:48.82,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Gasparo!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.82,0:05:51.28,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Have this woman removed at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.28,0:05:56.25,Default,Gasparo,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I'm afraid I can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.01,0:06:01.84,Default,Gasparo,0,0,0,,Lady Lucia currently holds \Nthe power of the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.84,0:06:03.24,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,Why, I never!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.24,0:06:07.10,Default,Gasparo,0,0,0,,Men, escort the queen to her chambers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.10,0:06:08.55,Default,Gemma,0,0,0,,S-Stop right there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.40,0:06:11.01,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,There you have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.30,0:06:15.10,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,I know you've just arrived, \Nbut please take your leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.80,0:06:18.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Will you not let me meet the king?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.81,0:06:23.69,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,The king is still too unwell \Nto see the queen of Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.40,0:06:31.53,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be leaving for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.53,0:06:35.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I look forward to meeting \Nagain in the near future.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.29,0:06:38.33,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Do forgive me for being a poor host.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.15,0:06:46.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I don't know if that letter of proxy \Nwas really written by the king,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.51,0:06:49.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but that woman is bad news.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.93,0:06:53.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Her magic rivals mine, or that of a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.98,0:06:55.00,Default,Pamyra,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.00,0:06:58.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I didn't expect to run into someone so shady.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.89,0:07:01.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I bet Oscar will get mad at me again.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.64,0:07:02.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Good grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.86,0:07:04.60,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Rivaling that of a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.60,0:07:07.23,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,You really met such a human?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.50,0:07:11.41,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,To be precise, Lady Tinasha \Nhas more magical power,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.41,0:07:14.32,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,but that's not the only measure \Nof someone's strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.61,0:07:17.47,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,I think retreating for now was the right move.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.47,0:07:20.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I wonder if her goal is \Nto take over the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.33,0:07:22.18,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.18,0:07:25.37,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,It looked like those soldiers \Nwere under her mind control.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.37,0:07:28.33,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,If so, she can take control in no time at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.33,0:07:29.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm stumped.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.85,0:07:31.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Just as the year's about to end...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.47,0:07:37.84,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I do think we need to get rid of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.31,0:07:39.81,Default,Pamyra,0,0,0,,Do you now?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.51,0:07:47.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Since she's so powerful, I'll need to \Ncome up with a plan to take her on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.11,0:07:50.26,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,She was a bona fide human, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.91,0:07:54.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,She couldn't really be a witch, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.09,0:07:58.17,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,There currently exist \Nthree witches in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.17,0:08:03.23,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,If we exclude the Witch of Silence, who \Nwe know is the king of Farsas' grandmother,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.23,0:08:05.38,Default,Pamyra,0,0,0,,that leaves two witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.38,0:08:09.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The Witch of the Water \Nand the Witch of the Forbidden Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.10,0:08:11.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I've never met either of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.84,0:08:15.05,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,You might be able to narrow it down \Nif you ask all the spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.05,0:08:18.22,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,The Witch of the Water \Nuses invisible spells, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.22,0:08:19.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Or so they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.27,0:08:25.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The Witch of the Forbidden Forest, \Non the other hand, uses psychological magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.58,0:08:27.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They both sound awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.69,0:08:36.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oh, right, Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.62,0:08:37.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.87,0:08:42.78,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Do you know the story of Akashia \Nand the first queen of Farsas?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.40,0:08:44.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.68,0:08:47.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There are no records left from that period.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.06,0:08:51.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They must have been lost at some point in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.36,0:08:56.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They say the first queen \Ngave Akashia to the founding king.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.05,0:08:57.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's news to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.06,0:09:03.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,All I know about Akashia is that an inhuman \Nbeing pulled it out of the Lake of Silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.47,0:09:05.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Who in the world told you that story?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.89,0:09:11.18,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A Farsas royal who studied abroad\N in Tuldarr four hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.18,0:09:15.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Our family has a long history \Nof eccentric characters.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.01,0:09:17.56,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm not sure how reliable that story is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.45,0:09:19.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll go get my clothes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.95,0:09:21.69,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,No, this suits me just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.25,0:09:31.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll stop if you want me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.97,0:09:33.02,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Now's your chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.62,0:09:36.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You don't need to stop...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.92,0:09:39.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That said, Oscar...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.84,0:09:40.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.30,0:09:45.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let me say this first, since I feel like \Nyou'll be mad if I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:46.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Out with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.58,0:09:52.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I-I think I'm going to have to fight \Nsomeone as strong as a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.59,0:09:59.05,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Go put on some clothes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.05,0:10:00.57,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We can talk after you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.88,0:10:04.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Um, it's fine, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.47,0:10:10.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Without my chastity, I {\i1}would{\i0} need \Na lot more power to use spirit magic...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.40,0:10:12.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I've got plenty of magic anyway—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.09,0:10:13.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Go get dressed!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.55,0:10:15.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I was the one being dumb and reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.81,0:10:18.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.09,0:10:28.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Am I going to spend my whole life \Nwithout making love to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.01,0:10:36.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So did you try asking \Nall the spirits whether she's a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.03,0:10:37.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's the thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.94,0:10:42.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,One of the spirits knows \Nthe Witch of the Forbidden Forest,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.34,0:10:45.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but he's currently gone missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.49,0:10:47.08,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Gone missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.53,0:10:52.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That raises the chances that this woman \Nis the Witch of the Forbidden Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.50,0:10:53.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.41,0:10:58.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,When two events happen at the same time, \Nyou should suspect that they're related.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.94,0:11:00.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If that missing spirit was still here,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.15,0:11:04.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,you could know whether she was \Nthe Witch of the Forbidden Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.89,0:11:08.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I suppose that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.10,0:11:13.24,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Could Tuldarr have some remaining \Nrecords of the witches?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.63,0:11:16.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Even if we find out their \Nnames or appearances,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.65,0:11:19.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,there are no records left of their practices.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.21,0:11:26.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Leonora, the witch I killed, was only \Nfirst recorded after she had died.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.67,0:11:27.95,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.31,0:11:31.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The only others who might know are Travis,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.25,0:11:34.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,as well as Lavinia, as a fellow witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.90,0:11:37.27,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll try reaching out to Lavinia.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.27,0:11:39.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't go asking Travis.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.13,0:11:41.28,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What? Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.28,0:11:42.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm sure it'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.97,0:11:46.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If she makes any moves, let me know at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.41,0:11:48.17,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What about a preemptive attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.17,0:11:49.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You can't be serious...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.12,0:11:51.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.55,0:11:55.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A witch can wage war \Nagainst an entire country by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.68,0:12:00.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If she intends to mobilize the nation \Nand start a war, we can't let that happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.06,0:12:03.02,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,We should strike before she's fully prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.53,0:12:08.29,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I understand your logic, but it \Nwon't be pretty if we cross that line.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.68,0:12:10.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It could affect the entire mainland.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.71,0:12:15.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.54,0:12:19.17,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Anyway, that's a no.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.49,0:12:21.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You always go overboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.58,0:12:23.88,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.22,0:12:33.06,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You never run out of annoying enemies, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.33,0:12:48.93,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the new year festivities \Nwent off without a hitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.93,0:12:49.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.00,0:12:52.98,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,The Gandona Founding Day \Ncelebrations are in two weeks,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.98,0:12:58.17,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,with Queen Tinasha's abdication \Nand your wedding two weeks after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.17,0:13:00.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sure is a hectic schedule.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.48,0:13:02.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But it's out of our hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.99,0:13:04.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You can retire for the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.84,0:13:05.76,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.46,0:13:13.06,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You can go back as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.20,0:13:15.89,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,You noticed me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.89,0:13:18.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It felt like I was being watched.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.60,0:13:20.02,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you acting on Tinasha's orders?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.33,0:13:21.32,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.32,0:13:23.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Did you find that missing spirit?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.87,0:13:25.34,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Not a trace.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.34,0:13:29.49,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,How dare he go off on his own \Nand worry Lady Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.49,0:13:34.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That aside, I received a reply \Nfrom Lavinia about the witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.39,0:13:38.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The description matches that of \Nthe Witch of the Forbidden Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.45,0:13:40.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Her name is Lucrezia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.40,0:13:42.48,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,It really {\i1}was{\i0} her!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.48,0:13:43.55,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,This sucks.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.87,0:13:47.02,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It says here that she shows \Nno interest in politics.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.02,0:13:49.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I wonder what could have changed her mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.73,0:13:53.22,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Humans change all the time, \Nso this is no different.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.50,0:13:57.39,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,The part I can't stand is the fact \Nthat she uses psychological magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.09,0:14:01.42,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,I'll be leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.04,0:14:10.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't stand a chance against \Nher psychological spells, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.42,0:14:14.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,What a headache.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.32,0:14:18.98,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I didn't expect a barrier inside \Nthe mirror, resulting in all this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.98,0:14:21.25,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,That's what you get for being greedy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.25,0:14:23.34,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.98,0:14:28.47,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It seems only half the mirror activated.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.13,0:14:32.33,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Leaving us with our unlikely ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.33,0:14:34.01,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,You had it coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.97,0:14:37.93,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Well, it'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.28,0:14:41.07,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I have many schemes at hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.07,0:14:43.14,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Let's go ahead with this one first.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.20,0:14:48.48,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.48,0:14:50.82,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,What is this before me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.04,0:14:55.93,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Oh, we received it as a gift for the new year.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.93,0:14:57.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Feel free to enjoy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.36,0:14:59.50,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,A-Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.50,0:15:01.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't be shy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.10,0:15:03.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm not one for sweets, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.76,0:15:06.42,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll dig right in!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.28,0:15:15.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That said, I want you to work \Ntwice as hard after you eat that...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.65,0:15:17.66,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Lazar?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.10,0:15:52.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This magic circle really is well-made.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.46,0:15:55.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I see that it mostly maintains\N its form with minimal magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.40,0:15:59.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and it amplifies upon activation \Nby absorbing the magic around it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.52,0:16:01.47,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.47,0:16:05.23,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,I wanted to send mages to areas \Nthey haven't been deployed,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.57,0:16:06.90,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,and this is what I came up with.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.90,0:16:10.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You might be able to apply this \Nfor hidden magic circles.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.01,0:16:15.21,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Queen Tinasha, I thought you were here \Nto discuss wedding plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.21,0:16:17.70,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oh, it completely slipped my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.25,0:16:21.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, are you in... here...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.21,0:16:24.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.69,0:16:26.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Itz! Make sure Lazar is okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.83,0:16:38.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.22,0:16:41.93,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}This spell structure and this hex...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.27,0:16:43.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've come across it somewhere...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.82,0:16:47.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Where's Akashia?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.11,0:16:49.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was tricked!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.07,0:16:50.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Itz!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.96,0:16:52.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Keep an eye on these two!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.36,0:16:53.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be right back!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.78,0:17:03.61,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Was there always a door here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.47,0:17:07.88,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,There's all sorts of \Nunexpected happenings this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.84,0:17:11.42,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Well, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.57,0:17:25.40,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Ow, that smarts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.40,0:17:29.13,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Any longer, and it might have \Nmelted me down to the bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.98,0:17:33.50,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,So this is why only royalty \Ncan wield this sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.13,0:17:38.18,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Well now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.18,0:17:41.74,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I should be safe to use \Nteleportation magic from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.73,0:17:45.50,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Long time no see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.82,0:17:47.46,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Where do you think you're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.46,0:17:49.53,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,My, oh my.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.53,0:17:52.10,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I didn't expect you to pick up on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.70,0:17:54.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Put that down on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.32,0:17:57.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,And the same goes for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.69,0:18:01.57,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Now that's a proposition that turns me on.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.57,0:18:03.35,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,But I have someone waiting for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.35,0:18:04.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Then die.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.37,0:18:11.06,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We will meet again soon,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.06,0:18:12.97,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Witch of the Azure Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.99,0:18:19.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Witch of the Azure Moon?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.09,0:18:29.06,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How's Lazar?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.64,0:18:30.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,He's doing well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.96,0:18:33.02,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Doan is looking after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.02,0:18:34.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.88,0:18:39.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt must be the one responsible \Nfor the attack on Legis.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.24,0:18:42.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Both of you had the same hex placed on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.50,0:18:45.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You almost fell into a coma like Legis did.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.80,0:18:48.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Luckily, I was familiar with the hex.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.52,0:18:53.20,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,However, he did succeed \Nin making off with Eleterria.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.75,0:18:56.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.81,0:19:01.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Look here, Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.68,0:19:03.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,First, you saved my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.48,0:19:04.53,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.13,0:19:09.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Back in the Dark Age, a mistake \Nlike this would mean the gallows.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.58,0:19:12.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Do you have any last words?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.95,0:19:14.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.14,0:19:15.58,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I should have been more cautious.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.58,0:19:18.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm usually the one getting \Nlectured, so this is kind of fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.02,0:19:23.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I really am glad that nothing \Nterrible happened to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.10,0:19:30.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt was after both halves of Eleterria, \Nso he probably won't use the orb right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.78,0:19:34.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,On the other hand, we'll need to \Ntighten up security on the other orb.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.77,0:19:36.88,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Should we just destroy it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.88,0:19:39.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,We have no idea what that might do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.34,0:19:42.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Will it be safe in the Tuldarr treasury?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.31,0:19:50.31,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'd like to think so, but I can't help but \Nworry after the abnormal actions he took.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.23,0:19:54.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt is an expert at reading minds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.92,0:19:57.20,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Perhaps not people in general,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.20,0:20:00.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but rather, it seems he knows \Nthe two of us very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.38,0:20:05.93,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Isn't that because he infiltrated \NFarsas Castle as Nephelli's attendant?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.35,0:20:07.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,He even spoke with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.72,0:20:12.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,He did, but it goes beyond \Nsomething so superficial.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.38,0:20:14.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,His knowledge is more intimate.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.57,0:20:15.56,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Intimate?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.94,0:20:19.23,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's probably the current me that he knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.35,0:20:22.50,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Which is why I can't continue like this...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.51,0:20:32.66,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.95,0:20:36.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.26,0:20:37.88,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Pleading for your life?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.51,0:20:41.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You really {\i1}are{\i0} planning to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.78,0:20:43.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.22,0:20:45.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,We haven't even gotten married yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.10,0:20:47.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Fine, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.63,0:20:50.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you kill me, do it after \Nour kids have grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.97,0:20:52.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll consider it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.41,0:22:37.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I've grown soft lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.50,0:22:40.22,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Especially after you got engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.22,0:22:43.34,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,But you've been that way \Never since you came to this age.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.34,0:22:45.37,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Or should I say you've become spineless?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.12,0:22:49.28,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's refreshing when you're brutally honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.22,0:22:55.02,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,But you know, she used to be \Na nice, honest, and sweet little girl,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.02,0:22:56.56,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,before her first coronation.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.01,0:23:00.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I couldn't still act like a child \Nafter becoming queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.84,0:23:10.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It seems Valt has seen through me with \Nshocking clarity ever since we first met.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.62,0:23:13.84,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But he won't continue to do as he pleases.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.28,0:23:17.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Before my private life, I am a queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.41,0:23:21.39,Default,Group,0,0,0,,Your wish is our command.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.39,0:23:23.08,Default,Group,0,0,0,,Our one and only queen.
